# Approval trust root and the code that verifies it.
# A repo writer who can change these can approve their own briefings, so these
# paths require review by the code owner regardless of who opens the PR.
#
# ⚠ AS OF rev 7 THIS FILE IS ADVISORY ONLY.
# The ruleset that would have enforced it was withdrawn: push rulesets are not
# available on a public repository, and "Restrict file paths" blocks the push
# outright rather than routing it through a PR -- which would have blocked the
# bot pushes the delivery pipeline depends on. main is currently unprotected.
#
# What actually holds today: the approval public key is anchored out-of-band by
# the repo secret ATLAS_APPROVAL_PUBKEY_FINGERPRINT, which a repo writer cannot
# change. The integrity of the VERIFIER CODE below is NOT protected; that needs
# data-push and code to live on separately protected refs, which is separate work.

